### 1. Core Shells & Scripting

#### PowerShell
*   **What it is:** A powerful Windows command-line shell and task-based scripting language built on the .NET framework, designed for automation and system management.
*   **Attacker Use Case:** Attackers frequently abuse PowerShell to launch **fileless attacks**, execute commands entirely in memory, and download malicious second-stage payloads directly from the internet.
*   **Blue Team Defense:** Defenders actively monitor PowerShell logs (specifically <layout>linkableSpan(text="Script Block Logging", intent="Learn about enabling PowerShell script block logging for security auditing")</layout> and Module Logging) to catch early indicators of compromise (IoCs), obfuscated code, and malicious script execution.

