### 2. Privilege Management

#### User Account Control (UAC)
*   **What it is:** A Windows security feature designed to prevent unauthorized privilege escalation by ensuring applications run in the context of a non-administrative account unless explicitly authorized.
*   **Why it matters:** It acts as a critical barrier against malware gaining full system-level access. Attackers constantly develop <layout>linkableSpan(text="UAC bypass techniques", intent="Read about common UAC bypass techniques and MITRE ATT&CK patterns")</layout> to silently elevate their permissions without triggering a user prompt.

